-- title:
--   Supersingular special-fibre points lie on the Gauss sheet
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K_1$ of $L((q))$ over $L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of the $q$-expansion field `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p` of $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of that rational function field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K_1$ compatibly, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K_1$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_1$ presented by: $f \in W_0$ iff $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((q))$ for power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $z$ be a point of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K₁ j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of the two affine charts, whose finite chart has coordinate ring the elements of $K_1$ integral over $A[j]$), let $\varpi z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section coming from $\varpi$ along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$, and assume $\varpi z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra mapping to $z$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the finite chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $p$. Writing $\mathfrak{y}$ for the prime ideal of $y$, the conclusion is that every element $s$ of the finite chart algebra whose image in $K_1$ is a non-unit of $W_0$ lies in $\mathfrak{y}$.
--
--   In the Deligne–Rapoport description, the special fibre of the integral model of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$ is a union of two copies of $X_1(M)$ in characteristic $p$ meeting exactly at the supersingular points; the centre of the Gauss valuation $W_0$ on the chart algebra is the generic point of one of these sheets, and the assertion is that a supersingular point of the special fibre lies on that sheet. It feeds the subsequent computations of the inertia group at such a point used in the level-lowering input.
